<title>BELGIUM: Ford Belgium 1996 profit edges up.</title>
<headline>Ford Belgium 1996 profit edges up.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in million Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				406.78 vs    397.00</p>
<p>    Turnover			     22,827.10 vs 18,958.74</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			  516.14 vs    508.66</p>
<p>    Provision for taxes		   109.36 vs    111.66</p>
<p>    Gross dividend (francs/share)	 200  vs    n/a</p>
<p>NOTE - Ford Motor Company (Belgium) SA is responsible for the sale of Ford vehicles in Belgium and Luxembourg.  </p>
<p>In 1996 sales of new vehicles rose by 17 percent to 49,348 from 42,018 in 1995. Ford said in a statement the rise was in part due to extra demand inspired by Brussels' biennial car show.</p>
<p>The market rose by 10 percent for both cars and for medium and light utility vehicles. Ford increased its market share in Belgium and Luxembourg by 10 percent.</p>
<p>Ford said that in 1997 it would continue and extend its strategy of security.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
